{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-8f15b867ca6366a11d7d","statement":"If $M$ is a cuspidal (resp. strongly cuspidal) $\\V$-module then $\\hM$ is a cuspidal (resp. strongly cuspidal) $\\AV$-module.","source_id":"arXiv:2006.05618","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"d67df529aad69715a29439f61dc85718efa32e1fa84a52bc7e57b1962be89a4e","kind":"theorem","label":"Theorem 12","ref_key":"cusp","name":"","order":36,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.05618","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"7a371cd4c4c4aab52c55e2601a17686e0fafc32675edff2c56797ff902f10ac0","line":961,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:19:35+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":123,"math_hints":11}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2006.05618","title":"Classification of simple strong Harish-Chandra $W(m,n)$-modules","abstract":"We classify all simple strong Harish-Chandra modules for the Lie superalgebra $W(m,n)$. We show that every such module is either strongly cuspidal or a module of the highest weight type. We construct tensor modules for $W(m,n)$, which are parametrized by simple finite-dimensional $gl(m,n)$-modules and show that every simple strongly cuspidal $W(m,n)$-module is a quotient of a tensor module. Finally, we realize modules of the highest weight type as simple quotients of the generalized Verma modules induced from tensor modules for $W(m-1,n)$.","authors":["Yuly Billig","Vyacheslav Futorny","Kenji Iohara","Iryna Kashuba"],"year":"2020","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.05618","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"C":"{\\mathbb C}","Z":"{\\mathbb Z}","N":"{\\mathbb N}","K":"{\\mathbb K}","R":"{\\mathcal R}","A":"{\\mathcal A}","AV":"{\\mathcal {AV}}","F":"{\\mathcal F}","V":"{\\mathcal V}","LL":"{\\mathcal L}","HH":"{\\mathcal H}","h":"{\\mathfrak h}","n":"{\\math